WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
This simplified study map moves between covenant, communal conduct, and judgment, with 5:41–50 as its proposed hinge.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
7 thematic movements in this study arrangement. The labels summarize passages; they are not Quran translations.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The opening sets obligations. The closing returns to food, the heavenly Table, and testimony before God. Compare the frame without reducing its differences.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Covenants involving earlier communities appear early; later passages revisit beliefs and responses concerning Jesus. The comparison is broad and thematic.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The account of violence and its legal aftermath can be read beside later

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
instructions governing conduct among communities. This pairing belongs to the site’s simplified map.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Within 5:41–50, verse 5:48 discusses revelation, differing laws and ways, and striving in good deeds. The diagram presents this as a proposed interpretive hinge.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.000
The connecting marks gather into nested rings. Their symmetry visualizes this reading; it does not establish the reading by itself.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Read 5:48 with its surrounding discussion of judgment and revelation. What does the surrounding context add?
